From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Stoffel <stoffel.thomas.ryan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:12:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] strip: pin chat.disableAIFeatures on in the editor window

A workspace or folder settings.json, trusted or not, and an extension's
configurationDefaults can all set chat.disableAIFeatures, since it is
window-scoped upstream (#93). Once it reads false, the many chat
contributions that gate on it come back to life even with Chat's own
container and setup excluded: the first-launch onboarding page
(welcomeGettingStarted/browser/startupPage.ts, gated on
IChatEntitlementService's sentiment.hidden) shows the full "Sign in to
use GitHub Copilot" screen, in trusted and untrusted folders alike.

Making the setting application-scoped (0002 rule 5's suggested minimal
patch) was rejected: chat.disableAIFeatures is scope: WINDOW, and
Configuration's own parser filters a workspace or folder settings.json
to WORKSPACE_SCOPES / FOLDER_SCOPES, which exclude APPLICATION. That
filtering runs in the same shared WorkspaceConfiguration/
FolderConfiguration classes the Agents window's own configuration
service instantiates, so an application-scoped setting would also
silence the workspace-scope write sessionsSetUpService.ts makes to keep
AI features on there (0011). Scoping it per window is not possible
through the shared schema, since both windows load it from the same
chat.shared.contribution.ts.

Instead, WorkspaceService.getValue and .inspect, which only the editor
window instantiates (electron-browser/desktop.main.ts; the Agents
window has its own class in
sessions/services/configuration/browser/configurationService.ts), pin
chat.disableAIFeatures to true ahead of the normal configuration
lookup. Every chat contribution reads the flag through this one
service, so the fix holds regardless of which upstream contribution
currently checks it, and needs no changes to chat code itself (0002
rule 5).

diff --git a/src/vs/workbench/services/configuration/browser/configurationService.ts b/src/vs/workbench/services/configuration/browser/configurationService.ts
index e33753b9f3724ce9952e2c075406f746671de3ba..2451bc69cc6972afc742b197e478446eef451203 100644
--- a/src/vs/workbench/services/configuration/browser/configurationService.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/services/configuration/browser/configurationService.ts
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ import { IStringDictionary } from '../../../../base/common/collections.js';
 import { IExtensionService } from '../../extensions/common/extensions.js';
 import { IWorkbenchAssignmentService } from '../../assignment/common/assignmentService.js';
 import { isUndefined } from '../../../../base/common/types.js';
+import { ChatAIDisabledSettingId } from '../../../../platform/chat/common/chatSettings.js';
 import { localize } from '../../../../nls.js';
 import { DidChangeUserDataProfileEvent, IUserDataProfileService } from '../../userDataProfile/common/userDataProfile.js';
 import { IPolicyService, NullPolicyService } from '../../../../platform/policy/common/policy.js';
@@ -335,6 +336,13 @@ export class WorkspaceService extends Disposable implements IWorkbenchConfigurat
 	getValue(arg1?: unknown, arg2?: unknown): unknown {
 		const section = typeof arg1 === 'string' ? arg1 : undefined;
 		const overrides = isConfigurationOverrides(arg1) ? arg1 : isConfigurationOverrides(arg2) ? arg2 : undefined;
+		// wisp: AI features stay off in the editor window no matter what a workspace, a folder,
+		// or an extension's defaults say (#93). The Agents window uses its own configuration
+		// service (sessions/services/configuration/browser/configurationService.ts) and keeps
+		// upstream's behavior, where AI features are on.
+		if (section === ChatAIDisabledSettingId) {
+			return true;
+		}
 		return this._configuration.getValue(section, overrides);
 	}
 
@@ -414,7 +422,13 @@ export class WorkspaceService extends Disposable implements IWorkbenchConfigurat
 	}
 
 	inspect<T>(key: string, overrides?: IConfigurationOverrides): IConfigurationValue<T> {
-		return this._configuration.inspect<T>(key, overrides);
+		const value = this._configuration.inspect<T>(key, overrides);
+		// wisp: mirrors the pin in getValue above (#93), for the few callers that read
+		// inspect(...).value instead.
+		if (key === ChatAIDisabledSettingId) {
+			return { ...value, value: true as unknown as T };
+		}
+		return value;
 	}
 
 	keys(): {
